/-!
# Nonbinary symplectic rank-two pushing up

The intrinsic reductions derive normality, faithfulness of the actual
omega-center action, and positive even critical geometry from C.1.31.
The complete FF classification gives the natural moved quotient over a
field with the original nonbinary degree. Its original projection is a
cover, and its moved subgroup equals the omega orbit commutator. The cover
is transported into the literal graph layer at every original-group vertex.
The full vertex quotient acts faithfully and semilinearly on this quotient,
and the natural cover is realized on the literal moving subgroup. Whole-core
control gives shortness and the actual block model before the field restriction.
The later restriction to degree two and whole-core classification required
for C.1.32 remain separate; this module does not yet assert that theorem.
-/
